             <details class="solution"><summary>Solution</summary>
               <p>Let \(m = \min\{d^{\top} H(p) d : |d| = 1\}\). The minimum exists because the unit circle is compact and the quadratic form is continuous, and \(m > 0\) by hypothesis. Assuming Assumption 2.1 of Lesson L06, and with \(\nabla f(p) = 0\), Theorem 3.1 gives \(f(p + sd) - f(p) \ge \tfrac12 s^2 m - 2s^2\omega(|s|) = s^2\bigl(\tfrac12 m - 2\omega(|s|)\bigr)\) for every unit \(d\), which is positive for every \(s \ne 0\) with \(\omega(|s|) < m/4\). That threshold does not depend on \(d\). The statement is about small steps, since \(\omega(|s|) \to 0\) is a limit, and it says nothing about a fixed step such as \(s = 0.1\) unless the threshold is checked for that step.</p>
